boswas-bootsplash (3.0~alpha1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Release 3.0~alpha1 (Boswas OS v3 Alpha).
  * Fill the display buffer again after the first mode-set; the screen
    stayed black, apart from the ring, after a driver had replaced the
    firmware frame buffer.
  * Follow a change of graphics device from inside the sandbox: the
    supervisor opens the new device and passes it to the worker.
  * One boot screen at a time (a lock); a second start leaves a running
    one alone, and a supervisor cleans up only after its own worker, also
    after the switch to the real root.
  * quit ends a boot screen that does not answer; the hand-over unit no
    longer depends on the pid file. Emergency and rescue mode end the
    boot screen.
  * Never put a console back into text mode, or take a display back, once
    a graphical session runs there.
  * Put raw keyboard mode back when the console is reset during boot.
  * Stop drawing on a legacy frame buffer that has been replaced.
  * initramfs: copy the DRM drivers in the hook (Debian's initramfs-tools
    has no FRAMEBUFFER option); wait for a display in the start unit.

 -- Boswas OS Platform Team <os-platform@boswas.invalid>  Mon, 16 Nov 2026 06:01:55 +0000

boswas-bootsplash (1.0~alpha3) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: the Boswas OS boot, disk-unlock and shutdown screen
    (boswas-bootsplashd, boswas-bootsplash), written in Rust. It replaces
    the Plymouth theme of boswas-branding and Plymouth itself.
  * Damage-tracked software rendering on DRM/KMS dumb buffers, with a
    legacy frame buffer fallback; artwork, glyphs and colours (Boswas UI
    tokens) embedded at build time.
  * Passphrase prompt for encrypted disks: started in the initramfs,
    called by /lib/cryptsetup/askpass through a Plymouth-compatible client
    that exists only inside the initramfs; a systemd password agent for
    later requests; the text console as the fallback in every failure case.
  * The daemon drops privileges once running (no_new_privs, Landlock,
    capabilities) and a supervisor restores the console if it dies.

 -- Boswas OS Platform Team <os-platform@boswas.invalid>  Sun, 15 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
